From cb9959ab5f99611d27a06586add84811fe8102dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 11:18:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: enforce HE/EHT cap/oper consistency
Git-commit: cb9959ab5f99611d27a06586add84811fe8102dc
Patch-mainline: v7.1-rc7
References: CVE-2026-53257 bsc#1269249

[ backport note: move the check to nl80211_calculate_ap_params() since
  the upstream commit a384ae969902 hasn't been backported on SL-16.1 ]

Xiang Mei reports that mac80211 could crash if eht_cap is set
but eht_oper isn't. Rather than fixing that for the individual
user(s), enforce that both HE/EHT have consistent elements.

Reported-by: Xiang Mei <xmei5@asu.edu>
Fixes: 22c64f37e1d4 ("wifi: mac80211: Update MCS15 support in link_conf")
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260603091812.101894-2-johannes@sipsolutions.net
Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/wireless/nl80211.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -6395,6 +6395,12 @@ static int nl80211_calculate_ap_params(s
 	const struct element *rates;
 	const struct element *cap;
 
+	if (!!params->he_cap != !!params->he_oper)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	if (!!params->eht_cap != !!params->eht_oper)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	rates = cfg80211_find_elem(WLAN_EID_SUPP_RATES, ies, ies_len);
 	nl80211_check_ap_rate_selectors(params, rates);
 
